    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The test tree only contains the one acceptance test class, and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation so that a repeated `POST /api/owners` carrying an already-seen `Idempotency-Key` returns the originally created owner with **200** instead of creating a duplicate (which the identity/household checks would otherwise reject with 409).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (no Spring MVC controllers), the change is:\n\n**New function classes** (`rest/function/owner/`):\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 a component-scanned singleton Spring bean mapping key \u2192 created owner id, injected into functions by type. First-write-wins (`putIfAbsent`).\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 new **entry step**. Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header via `ServerHttpConnection` (absent/blank \u2192 treated as no key). On a hit to a live (non-soft-deleted) owner it sends that owner with `ResponseEntity.ok(dto)` and stops. Otherwise it takes the `create` flow (`@Flow(\"create\")`) to run the normal pipeline.\n- `CreateFlow` \u2014 single-method flow interface; not calling it short-circuits after the idempotent response is sent.\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 runs after `SaveOwner` (owner has its id) and records the key \u2192 id mapping; a no-op when no key was supplied.\n\n**YAML wiring** (`officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`):\n- Added `idempotency` as the first step with `outputs: { create: validate }`, so the existing `validate \u2192 \u2026 \u2192 save \u2192 audit` chain is now the `create` branch.\n- Inserted `record` between `audit` and `respond`.\n- Both new steps carry `govern: [ transaction ]`, consistent with the surrounding pipeline (the hit path reads the owner and maps it under the same transactional/persistence scope).\n\nThe idempotent response mirrors `RespondWithOwnerCreated`'s DTO enrichment (`bulkSignupWarning`, `possibleDuplicate`) for consistency, differing only in the 200 status and no `Location` header.\n\nNotes on correctness reasoning I verified along the way: `@Flow(\"name\")` requires a single-method interface (flow name = the annotation value, matched exactly against the YAML `outputs` key); all Spring beans are exposed to functions by type by the starter; `findById` in the active `spring-data-jpa` profile returns `null` when absent; and existing acceptance tests already rely on created owners being visible to later requests within a test's transaction, which is what the hit-path load depends on.",
