    "probe_text": "I now have the complete pipeline. Here's the full, ordered account of what happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** (`owners.POST.yml` \u2192 `authorize`): caller must satisfy `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`, else the request is denied.\n\nA single write transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`) spans every step from `idempotency` through `respond`, committing once at the end.\n\n## Ordered pipeline\n\n**1. `CheckIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header (trimmed; blank = absent).\n- *Side-effect / short-circuit:* if the key maps to a stored owner that still exists and is **not** soft-deleted, it returns that original owner with **200** (mapping the DTO, attaching bulk-signup warning and possible-duplicate info) and the rest of the pipeline never runs. Otherwise it takes the `create` flow.\n\n**2. `ValidateOwner`** \u2014 binds `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (the only body read) and validates, in this order:\n- Normalizes address: normalizes `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, flat `address`; composes the stored `address` from structured lines when `addressLine1` is present, else the flat address (mutates the request).\n- **Required-field check** (after normalization) \u2014 collects blanks among `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`; if any \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (**400**, lists offending fields).\n- **Telephone** \u2192 normalized to E.164; unparseable \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (**400**). Stores normalized value.\n- **Email** (optional) \u2014 if present: lower-cased/trimmed; syntactic check \u2192 `InvalidEmailException` (**400**); domain against disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (**400**). Stores normalized value.\n- **Postcode** (optional) \u2014 if present: must be 4 digits \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**); if the city maps to a known region, must fall in that region's range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**). Stores trimmed value.\n- Publishes the validated/normalized body for later steps.\n\n**3. `CheckIdentityUnique`** \u2014 over all **non-soft-deleted** owners:\n- Exact identity duplicate (`telephone | email | householdId`) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n- Household duplicate (same `householdId` from `lastName`+`postcode`) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**), **unless** the request sets `sharesHousehold: true`. Owners without a postcode have no household, so only the exact-identity rule applies.\n\n**4. `CheckCityCapacity`** \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive, trimmed; counts **all** owners, deleted included); if \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n**5. `ResolveRegistrationDate`** \u2014 resolves effective date = supplied date or server today.\n- Supplied date after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**); back-dating allowed.\n- Rolls weekends/listed 2026 holidays forward to the next business day. Publishes the adjusted date.\n\n**6. `CheckDailyLimit`** \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the adjusted date; if \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n\n*(Steps 7\u201311 are entity-building side-effects, no more rejections.)*\n\n**7. `BuildOwner`** \u2014 maps the DTO to a new `Owner`, overriding its registration date with the adjusted business-day date.\n\n**8. `AssignHousehold`** \u2014 sets deterministic `householdId` (SHA-256 of normalized `lastName`+`postcode`); left null when no postcode.\n\n**9. `AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode, hash from telephone+lastName); on collision with an existing code, appends `-<n>` (smallest n \u2265 2) to make it unique.\n\n**10. `AssignMembershipNumber`** \u2014 sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of the registration date's fiscal year (Jul 1\u2013Jun 30).\n\n**11. `AssignNamesakeCount`** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing this owner's first+last name (case-insensitive), before this owner is saved.\n\n**12. `SaveOwner`** \u2014 persists the owner (`ownerRepository.save`), assigning its id.\n\n**13. `AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 emits an `AUDIT` log line (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber).\n\n**14. `RecordIdempotencyKey`** \u2014 if the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records it against the new owner's id (no-op otherwise).\n\n**15. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto`, attaches `bulkSignupWarning`, computes `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (suppressed for declared household members), and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. The transaction commits here.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: the identity/uniqueness check (step 3) skips soft-deleted owners, but the city-capacity, daily-limit, and namesake counts (steps 4, 6, 11) count **all** rows including soft-deleted ones \u2014 an inconsistency in what \"existing owner\" means across the checks."
